																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13930512/roland-the-headless-thompson-gunner">Roland The Headless Thompson Gunner</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843968">
									

<p>The idea of a vengeance-driven headless specter has been around for a long time, although one mister horseman is by far the most well-known. I like the idea of a (relatively) modern take, and Warren Zevon came through to give me a good starting point, as the song already contains the basics for a good story. Plus, it's a good match for my signature mix of weirdness and character-driven stories.</p>
<p><a href="https://youtu.be/wRWCK9zGynA">https://youtu.be/wRWCK9zGynA</a></p>
<p>I'm hoping to tell the initial history of the anomaly and its assumed source in the description and logs, and how it hunted down its targets in conprocs and logs. For instance, detailing the response to a manifestation and how to not get shot by it, and which specific types of areas are most likely to have the thing appear.</p>
<p>As for the rest of the story, after it gets revenge I think it would be neat if the headless gunner shut down for a while. Formerly a mercenary, then driven to seek out revenge for itself, without any sort of personal gain it would just&#8230; stop. Until something awakens it again, and the eternal Thompson gunner learns to fight for other's sake. This I would probably explore through addenda and in-universe page revisions.</p>
<p>Thoughts? Anything I can explain further? Any response is appreciated greatly.</p>

							</div>

								
					
