<p>Honestly, at the moment this idea seems rather barebones. The central narrative here seems to be more of a description of how you are going to structure the article, rather than how you plan to tell an interesting story.</p>
<p>Furthermore, an arbitrary hook such as it having no control over its abilities and it being &quot;cute&quot;, doesn't particularly pull me in as we have far better articles (Like most of the Wilson's Wildlife stuff) that have a strong narrative to carry the article.</p>
<p>I would suggest you perhaps read some more recent wildlife-focused articles to help you understand how to incorporate a narrative into a piece like this.</p>
<p>Good luck</p>

