			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843950">
									

<p>A slight revision I made as a further development of this idea. I took out the part of the Obskuracorps but not sure if it would have been better to try and fit it in some how.</p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> History, Ghost</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A group of ex-nazis with a Panzer III are given the ability to spawn an entire division of ghost tanks after being recovered by SCP agents during a mission.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">**Central&nbsp;Narrative:**</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">**Central&nbsp;Narrative:**</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>In 1944, a group of german tank crew abandon the nazi cause and fled into the wilderness with a Panzer III. They survive by scavenging for food and going on raids against villages for supplies, unaware that the war is over and unsure of what is to become of them if they surrender, the tank crew refuse to return to the post-wwii Europe.</p>
<p>As time goes on, dissidence begins to grow in each of them against the former regime they served, throwing away their black and red armband, scratching off symbols of the old regime and discard anything else that has little functional purpose such as decorations, uniform insignia, etc keeping only the necessary items needed for survival.</p>
<p>During a containment breach at a nearby facility, a massive, bottomless sinkhole is formed taking the tank along with her crew with it to the bottom. Surprisingly, they survive the fall but find themselves in a world similar to our own, a damp, dark, cold world lacking any source of light. The hole they arrived from now appears as a tiny white dot surrounded by a sky of total darkness. As the group ventures throughout this “underworld,” they discover that it’s populated entirely by dark, shadowy beings that bear a disfigured, grainy, slender silhouette of a human. Worst yet is that they seem to be on the hunt for the tank crew.</p>
<p>Looking for a way out and forced to survive in this new world against these creatures, the tank crew utilize what limited ammunition and supply they have left on them to ensure the safety of their survival. Eventually, the tank that they utilized began to slowly change, with deep scratch marks being discovered both inside and outside the tank. The tank crew were ready to abandon the tank thinking that it was beginning to wear down until the radio man discovered that using the radio at a certain frequency would spawn a massive tank army consisting of only the limited WWII German tanks built during that era, with mighty caliber guns capable of toppling the deadliest war machines ever built and armour that could withstand the might of Zeus.</p>
<p>Decades later, an investigation into the sinkhole would commence by SCP agents. After multiple explorations, the panzer crew would be discovered and brought back to the surface, hands in the air appearing as though they haven’t aged a day since 1944. After reappearing from the underworld, the tank crew would utilize their tank army as a show of defiance against their new captors, only to realize that the former tank army that was made of the toughest armour had become a hazey, transparent division. Objects would come and go through the ghost's armour as tank shells would come roaring, crashing into the ground leaving no bodies to be found and only a crater in it’s spot. The screams of horrors by soldiers being gunned down and mutilated would play as they rolled past, deafening the hollowing engines of the tanks.</p>
<p>The tank crew would eventually be captured by MTF-Mu-13 and held in captivity by SCP researchers putting an end to their escape. Days later, multiple reports of “ghost tanks” would appear throughout Europe and North Africa, firing upon civilian homes, shopping centers, gas stations and random buildings leaving destruction and tens to hundreds of casualties with zero traces of the ghosts left. An interview conducted on the tank crew would show similarities in both their journey in the underworld and the aforementioned incidents in terms of behaviour, actions and locations.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

